            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R3-e2e-validate-tolerance",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "engine/skills/registry_lock_e2e_test.go:395-408",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "The real-tree validate e2e test now accepts exit 1 as long as every stderr line starts with '[APPROVAL_'. An empty stderr with exit 1, or a blank line, would produce a failing assertion only by accident (empty line fails the prefix check), but the test no longer proves validate exits 0 on a clean tree, and it does not assert that at least one approval finding exists when exit is 1. This weakens the regression signal for non-approval failures that print multi-line details.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/skills/registry_lock_e2e_test.go:395-408"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "R3-reader-double-symlink-dir",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "engine/skills/export_test.go:127-158",
                "severity": "SUGGESTION",
                "claim": "The test double ReadSkillTree uses Lstat on the skill directory and WalkDir, so a skill directory that is itself a symlink gives a failure ('not a directory'). The adapter contract test does not cover a symlinked skill root, so the double and adapter could diverge there unnoticed.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/skills/export_test.go:127-158",
                  "engine/skills/adapter_contract_test.go:64-105"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 11 changed paths; the baseline-removal tests are replaced by digest, gate, store, and classify tests covering order independence, per-file binding, version 1 stale handling, unverifiable entries, and missing-SKILL.md set-aside.",
              "Deleted approval_nil_baseline_test.go tests behavior (nil baseline lookup) that the candidate removes along with the baseline, so no coverage gap is left for it.",
              "No blocker or critical regressions are evident from the test changes alone."
            ]
          }
        }
      }
